<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="JirAI: Issue details and editing" id="Jira-Issue-Details-and-Editing">

    <primary-label ref="jirai"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Open: select an issue in the <control>JirAI</control> tool window and press <shortcut>Enter</shortcut></p>
        <p>Details menu: right-click the details tab for <control>Refresh</control> and <control>Hide Fields…</control></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Read an issue's fields, edit them in place, move the issue through its workflow, and manage attachments, links and child work items.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Edit fields in place, change status, and manage attachments, links and child work items.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Read and edit Jira Cloud issue fields in JetBrains IDEs with JirAI: in-place edits, workflow transitions, attachments, issue links and child work items.</web-summary>

    <p>The details tab shows one issue's fields and lets you change most of them without opening Jira.</p>

    <chapter title="Open the issue details" id="details-view">
        <p>In the <control>JirAI</control> tool window, select an issue and press <shortcut>Enter</shortcut>, double-click it, or right-click it and choose <control>Open Details</control>.</p>
        <p>The details tab opens in the tool window, named after the issue key, and the issue's <control>Timeline</control> tab opens in the editor.</p>
        <p>The header shows the key and summary, with a <control>Timeline ↗</control> link that opens the issue timeline.</p>
        <!-- planned-image src="jirai_issue_details.png" alt="Issue details tab with the type icon, the parent link and the Breakdown section" -->
        <p>The tab lists the standard fields, such as <control>Status</control>, <control>Assignee</control>, <control>Reporter</control>, <control>Priority</control>, <control>Type</control>, <control>Parent</control>, <control>Due date</control>, <control>Labels</control>, <control>Components</control> and <control>Fix versions</control>, followed by the custom fields.</p>
        <list>
            <li><p>Each field is shown according to the type Jira declares for it.</p></li>
            <li><p>The <control>Type</control> row shows the issue type icon.</p></li>
            <li><p>A field of a type JirAI cannot show yet reads <control>Not shown here</control>, with an <control>Open in Jira</control> link.</p></li>
            <li><p>Fields that Jira declares without a specific type, such as <control>Rank</control>, are left out.</p></li>
        </list>
        <p>To hide custom fields you do not need, see <a href="Jira-Field-Visibility.topic">Hide custom fields</a>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Edit fields in place" id="inline-editing">
        <p>Click a field value to change it.</p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Summary">Edit the text in place.</def>
            <def title="Priority">Choose a priority from the list.</def>
            <def title="Assignee">Search for a person, or click <control>Assign to me</control>.</def>
            <def title="Labels, Components, Fix versions">Add or remove values; you can filter the list or type a new label.</def>
            <def title="Due date">Pick a date, or clear it.</def>
            <def title="Parent">Search all projects by key or summary to choose a new parent, or choose <control>Clear parent</control>.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>To open the parent work item, click <control>Open ↗</control> beside the <control>Parent</control> field.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Change the status" id="workflow-transitions">
        <procedure title="Move an issue through its workflow" id="transition-proc">
            <step>
                <p>Click the <control>Status</control> value.</p>
                <p>The list shows the transitions your Jira workflow allows from the current status.</p>
                <!-- planned-image src="jirai_transition_popup.png" alt="Status dropdown listing the available workflow transitions" -->
            </step>
            <step><p>Choose a transition.</p></step>
            <step>
                <p>If the transition has a screen with fields, such as <control>Resolution</control>, fill them in the dialog that opens and confirm.</p>
                <p>The confirm button stays disabled while a required field is empty.</p>
                <!-- planned-image src="jirai_transition_screen.png" alt="Transition dialog asking for the required Resolution field" -->
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>A transition field JirAI cannot edit shows an <control>Open in browser</control> link, so that you can complete the transition in Jira.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Attachments" id="attachments">
        <list>
            <li><p>To attach files, click the paperclip (<control>Attach files…</control>) and choose the files, or drag files onto the <control>Attachments</control> section.</p></li>
            <li><p>Image attachments show a thumbnail when Jira provides one.</p></li>
            <li><p>Use the actions on an attachment to download it or delete it; deleting asks for confirmation.</p></li>
        </list>
        <p>On macOS and Windows, JirAI uses the operating system file dialog; on Linux, it uses the IDE file chooser.</p>
        <!-- planned-image src="jirai_attachments_links.png" alt="Attachments section with an image thumbnail, and the Linked issues section" -->
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Issue links" id="issue-links">
        <procedure title="Link two issues" id="link-issue-proc">
            <step><p>In the <control>Linked issues</control> section, click <control>Add link</control>.</p></step>
            <step><p>In the <control>Link Issue</control> dialog, choose the <control>Link type:</control>, for example <emphasis>blocks</emphasis> or <emphasis>relates to</emphasis>.</p></step>
            <step><p>Search for the other issue by key or summary, select it and confirm.</p></step>
        </procedure>
        <p>To remove a link, use <control>Remove link</control> on its row.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Child work items (Breakdown)" id="breakdown-section">
        <secondary-label ref="jirai_version"/>
        <p>The <control>Breakdown</control> section lists up to five child work items of the issue, sub-tasks included.</p>
        <list>
            <li><p>Click a child to open it in its own details tab.</p></li>
            <li><p>When there are more children, click <control>+N more ↗</control> or <control>More ↗</control> to open the full list in the <control>Breakdown</control> tab of the editor.</p></li>
            <li><p>Click <control>Add child</control> to create a child work item. See <a href="Jira-Create-Issues.topic" anchor="add-child">Create a child work item</a>.</p></li>
        </list>
        <p>For the full list, see <a href="Jira-Timeline-and-Description-Editor.topic" anchor="breakdown-tab">The Breakdown tab</a>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Refresh the details" id="details-refresh">
        <p>Right-click anywhere in the details tab, including on a field name, and choose <control>Refresh</control> to reload the issue from Jira.</p>
    </chapter>

